  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=-1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{′}(0)=0,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=A\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{7}x)-B\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{7}x).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=0$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n0=A\\sqrt{7}\\,⟹\\,A=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{7}x).\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
